import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 305 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Ye Fan vs. Gu Chensha: Oligarchic vs. Single-Log Comparison","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 305 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Ye Fan vs. Gu Chensha: Oligarchic vs. Single-Log Comparison","no":305,"module":2,"tags":["Shrouding the Heavens","Ye Fan","Gu Chensha","Dragon Talisman","Oligarchic vs. Single-Log","Protagonist Uniqueness"],"related":["30-Five Symbiotic Civilization Typology Overview","17-Plane Transcendent Standards","01-Anchor Symbiotic Civilization Manifesto"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0305_模块2-遮天-叶凡vs古尘沙.md","filePath":"en/0305_模块2-遮天-叶凡vs古尘沙.md"}'),a={name:"en/0305_模块2-遮天-叶凡vs古尘沙.md"};function o(r,e,l,h,c,d){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="entry-305-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-ye-fan-vs-gu-chensha-oligarchic-vs-single-log-comparison" tabindex="-1">Entry 305 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Ye Fan vs. Gu Chensha: Oligarchic vs. Single-Log Comparison <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-305-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-ye-fan-vs-gu-chensha-oligarchic-vs-single-log-comparison" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 305 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Ye Fan vs. Gu Chensha: Oligarchic vs. Single-Log Comparison&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Shrouding-the-Heavens System (Entry 18) | Benchmark base: Documents 30, 17, 01</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-between-two-ceilings-lies-a-whole-civilization-s-distance" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Between two ceilings lies a whole civilization&#39;s distance <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-between-two-ceilings-lies-a-whole-civilization-s-distance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Between two ceilings lies a whole civilization&#39;s distance&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the republican axiom of Myriad Races opposes tying civilization&#39;s survival to one person; on the five-tier protagonist-uniqueness-dependence scale, Gu Chensha = extreme / single-log type, Ye Fan = medium / oligarchic type. This entry uses Dragon Talisman&#39;s Gu Chensha as contrast to locate Ye Fan&#39;s position in the Myriad-Realms protagonist genealogy. The law-first axiom reminds: comparison is not about combat power, but about civilization structure. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = medium (oligarchic civilization). The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Two civilizations&#39; energy-waste forms differ:</p><ul><li><strong>Gu Chensha (single-log)</strong>: first from antiquity, casually creates worlds, all beings &quot;are made dragons&quot;; energy all tied to him alone; the stronger he gets, the more idle all beings are</li><li><strong>Ye Fan (oligarchic)</strong>: depends on a strong-one group (Ye Fan + peer emperors + trusted line), energy dispersed in a small circle, still has some institutional prototype</li></ul><p>Comparison conclusion: Ye Fan&#39;s energy waste is slightly lighter — he at least is not the sole pillar, but outside the small circle is still idle.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Single-log and oligarchic regression mechanisms:</p><ol><li><strong>Gu Chensha</strong>: if he disappears, all beings have no self-rescue ability; regression probability approaches one</li><li><strong>Ye Fan</strong>: if the oligarchic group exits as a whole, civilization still regresses, but with slightly more buffer — changing people within the group is slightly more possible than replacing Gu Chensha</li><li>Both share: neither writes order into institutions; both rely on &quot;strong ones watching&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predation form comparison:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Gu Chensha (single-log)</th><th>Ye Fan (oligarchic)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>All beings&#39; position</td><td>Objects being made dragons</td><td>The protected</td></tr><tr><td>Transmission way</td><td>Antiquity&#39;s first pities</td><td>Trusted line selects heirs</td></tr><tr><td>Governance power</td><td>All to Gu Chensha</td><td>Shared within oligarchic group</td></tr><tr><td>Myriad Ranks subjectivity</td><td>Fully outsourced</td><td>Slight participation but minimal</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Ye Fan&#39;s predation is more &quot;dispersed,&quot; but essentially still takes civilization&#39;s fate from Myriad Ranks&#39; hands.</p><p>Single-log and oligarchic also have a key difference: tolerance for &quot;exit.&quot; If Gu Chensha disappears, the world instantly loses its engine; if Ye Fan and his circle disappear, the world will be chaotic for a while, but residual order can barely hold. This difference looks small, actually decides two civilizations&#39; historical resilience. Oligarchic civilization is like a team propped by a few starters; when starters are injured it can still barely play a few games; single-log civilization is a team with only one player; he leaves the field and it completely stalls. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s networked civilization requires every position to have qualified backups — anyone exits, the match goes on.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Single-Log (Gu Chensha)</th><th>Oligarchic (Ye Fan)</th><th>Network (Heng Yuan Zhou)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dependence</td><td>Extreme</td><td>Medium</td><td>Extremely low</td></tr><tr><td>Civilization form</td><td>Single-log</td><td>Oligarchic</td><td>Networked</td></tr><tr><td>Order basis</td><td>One person</td><td>Small circle</td><td>Institution + network</td></tr><tr><td>Exit risk</td><td>Civilization collapses</td><td>Turmoil</td><td>Unaffected</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Ye Fan is &quot;slightly better&quot; than Gu Chensha, but both are intrinsically distant from Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s networked civilization.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate two civilizations&#39; power concentration</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: remove &quot;Gu Chensha&quot; and &quot;Ye Fan and his group&quot; separately, observe collapse speed</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: civilization recovery time, Myriad Ranks&#39; self-rescue ability</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: conclusion — oligarchic collapses slightly slower than single-log, but still far slower than network&#39;s &quot;does not collapse&quot;</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency</strong>: Gu Chensha system (Dragon Talisman) high self-consistency (casual world creation but internal rules clear); Ye Fan system medium-low self-consistency</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk</strong>: Gu Chensha low risk; Ye Fan high risk</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: Gu Chensha = extreme; Ye Fan = medium</li></ul><p>Gu Chensha and Ye Fan also have an interesting contrast: Gu Chensha &quot;bears sins for all beings,&quot; Ye Fan &quot;suppresses chaos for all beings.&quot; Different form, same structure — both outsource responsibility that should be jointly borne by Myriad Ranks to one (or a group of) strong ones. Myriad Ranks in both stories are passive receivers. What Heng Yuan Zhou wants to break is precisely this &quot;outsourcing mentality&quot;: sins must be faced by Myriad Ranks themselves, turmoil must be governed by Myriad Ranks themselves; cannot be outsourced to any sage. The more outsourced, the less Myriad Ranks can self-rescue.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: single-log wastes on all beings being idle, oligarchic wastes outside the small circle</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: both take civilization&#39;s fate from Myriad Ranks&#39; hands</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo = high dependence / bestowed type, between Gu Chensha and Ye Fan</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: neither single-log nor oligarchic achieves Myriad-Ranks co-governance</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: only networked civilization can stably expand cross-multiverse</li></ul><p>Gu Chensha and Ye Fan also share a blind spot: both assume &quot;all beings need someone stronger.&quot; Gu Chensha bears sins for all beings, Ye Fan suppresses chaos for all beings, but neither asks whether all beings want to be treated this way. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s fundamental stance: all beings do not need to be done-for; what they need is ability and opportunity. Giving one person greater power to protect Myriad Ranks is inferior to giving Myriad Ranks enough ability to protect themselves.</p><ul><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Ye Fan is &quot;more like a normal civilization&quot; than Gu Chensha — because he still has peers, a faction, faction politics. But this is only picking the taller among dwarves: from &quot;one person saves the cosmos&quot; to &quot;a group saves the cosmos,&quot; what Heng Yuan Zhou wants is &quot;the cosmos saves itself.&quot;</p><p>Gu Chensha and Ye Fan, one is a single log, the other a few pillars; what Heng Yuan Zhou wants is the entire forest. A single log and pillars both look better than a forest, but only a forest remains a forest when any one tree falls.</p><p>In the final analysis, Shrouding-the-Heavens · Ye Fan vs. Gu Chensha described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./306_模块2-遮天-叶凡vs唐罗.html">Entry 306 · Ye Fan vs. Tang Luo</a> · <a href="./307_模块2-遮天-叶凡vs衡元宙.html">Entry 307 · Ye Fan vs. Heng Yuan Zhou</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/30-五种共生文明分型总览.html">30-Five Symbiotic Civilization Typology Overview</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',35)])])}const p=i(a,[["render",o]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
